## Blueprint

**Leaf**: Test-only leaf. Add test cases to `src/services/__tests__/conductor-pass.test.ts` covering the two terminal-status branches of the existing pin-clearing logic in `runConductorPass` (`src/services/conductor-pass.ts:113-120`) — pinning a mission whose status is `'converged'` and one whose status is `'abandoned'` must both (a) clear the pin (`setConductorTargetMission(project, null)` is called internally, verifiable via `getConductorTargetMission(project) === null` afterward) and (b) drive nothing (`ran: false`, `reason: 'target-cleared'`, zero `invokeCalls`). The existing test at line 151 ("pin a missing mission clears it lazily") only covers the *nonexistent row* case (`!row`); it does not exercise the `row.status === 'converged'` or `row.status === 'abandoned'` arms of the same `if` condition at conductor-pass.ts:115. This leaf closes that gap.

**File to edit**: `src/services/__tests__/conductor-pass.test.ts`, inside the `describe('runConductorPass — target pin', ...)` block (after the existing "pin a missing mission clears it lazily" test at line 162).

**How to build the two terminal fixtures**:
- Converged: forge a mission with one criterion (`forgeMission(project, { session: 's1', title: '...', criteria: ['c'] })`), then call `setCriterionMet(project, listCriteria(project, forged.missionId)[0].id, true)` (import `setCriterionMet` from `../mission-store`, alongside the already-imported `listCriteria`). `deriveCriterionAction`/status derivation (mission-store.ts:658-666) treats "≥1 criterion exists and all are met" as `converged`.
- Abandoned: forge a mission, then call `setMissionAbandoned(project, forged.missionId, Date.now())` (import `setMissionAbandoned` from `../mission-store`). This sets `abandonedAt`, and `deriveMissionStatus`/`getMission`'s status derivation reads `f.abandonedAt != null` as `'abandoned'` (mission-store.ts:658).

**Test shape** (two new `test(...)` blocks, following the exact pattern of the existing "pin a missing mission clears it lazily" test):

```ts
test('pin a converged mission clears the pin and drives nothing', async () => {
  addWatchedProject(project);
  setConductorEnabled(project, true);
  await forgeApprovedActive(); // an otherwise-actionable mission that must NOT be fallen back to
  const converged = await forgeMission(project, { session: 's1', title: 'already converged', criteria: ['c'] });
  setCriterionMet(project, listCriteria(project, converged.missionId)[0].id, true);
  expect(getMission(project, converged.missionId)?.status).toBe('converged');

  setConductorTargetMission(project, converged.missionId);
  const r = await runConductorPass(project, { invoke: okInvoke });
  expect(r.ran).toBe(false);
  expect(r.reason).toBe('target-cleared');
  expect(invokeCalls).toBe(0);
  expect(getConductorTargetMission(project)).toBe(null);
});

test('pin an abandoned mission clears the pin and drives nothing', async () => {
  addWatchedProject(project);
  setConductorEnabled(project, true);
  await forgeApprovedActive();
  const abandoned = await forgeApprovedActive2(); // or forgeMission with distinct title
  setMissionAbandoned(project, abandoned.missionId, Date.now());
  expect(getMission(project, abandoned.missionId)?.status).toBe('abandoned');

  setConductorTargetMission(project, abandoned.missionId);
  const r = await runConductorPass(project, { invoke: okInvoke });
  expect(r.ran).toBe(false);
  expect(r.reason).toBe('target-cleared');
  expect(invokeCalls).toBe(0);
  expect(getConductorTargetMission(project)).toBe(null);
});
```

(Use `forgeMission(project, { session: 's1', title: 'to be abandoned', criteria: ['c'] })` directly for the second fixture rather than reusing `forgeApprovedActive()` twice with the same title, to keep mission titles distinct for readability — actual titles are free-form, any non-colliding string works.)

Both tests must assert all four things the existing missing-mission test asserts (`ran`, `reason`, `invokeCalls`, and the pin actually clearing via `getConductorTargetMission`), since the leaf title explicitly calls out both "clears the pin" and "drives nothing" as the two behaviors under test.

**Imports to add** at the top of the test file: `setCriterionMet`, `setMissionAbandoned` from `../mission-store` (both already exported; `setCriterionMet` sits at mission-store.ts:431, `setMissionAbandoned` at mission-store.ts:313). `listCriteria` and `getMission` are already imported.

**Out of scope**: no change to `src/services/conductor-pass.ts` itself — the clearing logic (line 115-120) already exists and is believed correct; this leaf only proves it with tests. No change to `mission-store.ts`.

